Icon assets in this folder are copied from Bootstrap Icons v1.13.1
(https://icons.getbootstrap.com/), redistributed here under the MIT License.

The path data is unmodified. Only the SVG wrapper attributes were normalized
(viewBox="0 0 16 16", fill="#000", no width/height/class, single line) so the
files can be used as CSS mask images with `background: currentColor`.

Two groups of files are drawn locally for this project on the same 16x16 grid,
so their path data does not come from Bootstrap Icons:

- `print.svg` (the capture toolbar's "export PDF" button).
- The icon-only option row and thickness picker added on 2026-10-15
  (`weight-*` / `stroke-*` / `radius-*` / `head-*`): the upstream set has no
  line-weight, stroke-style, corner-radius or arrowhead-end glyphs. They re-use
  the family's conventions instead: 1px features with 0.5px round caps, and
  `fill-rule="evenodd"` where a shape needs an outline.

The remaining files added on 2026-10-15 still carry unmodified upstream path
data and are only renamed after the option they represent:

- `fill-outline.svg`     = `square.svg`
- `fill-translucent.svg` = `square-half.svg`
- `fill-solid.svg`       = `square-fill.svg`
- `alpha-light.svg`      = `droplet.svg`
- `alpha-medium.svg`     = `droplet-half.svg`
- `alpha-strong.svg`     = `droplet-fill.svg`
- `bold.svg`             = `type-bold.svg`

